# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

`rust (classify)` took 7m35s on #2650's pull request. That PR changed 4 card scripts, the engine and the AI, so stage 2 ran all three of its checks one after another. Measured locally on 4 cores (the runner has 4), with the head's build and a copy of it as the parent:

| Phase | Time | CPU |
|---|---|---|
| Stage 1 | 1.2 s | |
| Forced games, 4 scripts | 0–92 s | |
| 200 unforced games | 92–184 s | |
| Self-play, both builds side by side | 184–415 s | 784 CPU-s |
| Whole stage 2 | 419 s | 1561 CPU-s |

One self-play run alone takes 115 s (game `classify:1` alone takes 115 s). The self-play roughly doubled when #2575 doubled `AI_GATE_BUDGET` to 1200 nodes.

The job is CPU-bound, so no reordering on one runner reaches 5 minutes without playing fewer or weaker games, and weakening the check is not allowed. Done looks like this:

- **(a)** `jackioh classify --selfplay-side head|base --selfplay-dir <dir>` plays one side's self-play games into `<dir>/<side>` and stops.
- **(b)** `classify --parent-bin <p> --selfplay-dir <dir>` compares those two runs instead of playing them.
- **(c)** A person adds the CI job that plays each side on its own runner (see Open questions). Then each job stays under 5 minutes on #2650's diff: each self-play leg about 2.5 min, `rust (classify)` about 3.7 min.

Without the new flags the classifier behaves exactly as today.

